<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Rerank Methods</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Average</span>: Computes the average ranking position of each model across all questions. Models with lower average ranks are placed higher.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Borda Count</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Saari (1985)</a></cite>: Assigns each model a score based on its position in each ranking (with higher-ranked positions receiving more points). The final ranking is obtained by sorting models by total Borda score in descending order.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Copeland Method</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Saari and Merlin (1996)</a></cite>: For each pair of models, assigns <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math> for a win, <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> for a loss, and <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> for a tie. Each model’s net score is computed by summing across all pairwise comparisons. Higher net scores lead to higher ranks.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dodgson Method</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Brandt (2009)</a></cite>: Measures how many adjacent swaps in the rankings are needed to make each model a Condorcet winner. The fewer swaps required, the better the rank.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">IRV</span>(Instant-Runoff Voting) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Brandt (2009)</a></cite>: Iteratively eliminates the model with the fewest first-choice votes and redistributes the votes to remaining candidates, until one model remains. Final ranking is based on the order of elimination.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Kemeny-Young Method</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kemeny (1959)</a></cite>: Computes the total pairwise disagreement (Kemeny distance) between each possible ranking and all input rankings. The ranking that minimizes total disagreement is selected as the consensus.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Kendall Aggregation</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kendall (1948)</a></cite>: Enumerates all possible rankings and selects the one that maximizes the total Kendall tau correlation with the input rankings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spearman Aggregation</span>: Searches all permutations and selects the one that maximizes the sum of absolute Spearman correlations with the input rankings.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Supplementary experiment on Q1</h2>

<figure id="A6.T7" class="ltx_table">
