<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span>
Distribution of <span id="A6.T12.23" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pearson</span> and <span id="A6.T12.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Kendall</span> correlation coefficients between automated rankings and human ranking on the <span id="A6.T12.25" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Creative Writing</span> dataset. Each value reflects micro-level alignment computed per individual problem. The first six columns report the performance of individual LLMs, while the remaining columns correspond to various rank aggregation methods. Reported statistics include the Mean, standard deviation (<span id="A6.T12.26" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Std.</span>), minimum (<span id="A6.T12.27" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Min</span>), and the 25th, 50th (median), 75th percentiles, and maximum (<span id="A6.T12.28" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Max</span>) values across all problems. Abbreviations: <span id="A6.T12.29" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Avg</span> = average voting, <span id="A6.T12.30" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dod</span> = Dodgson, <span id="A6.T12.31" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cop</span> = Condorcet, <span id="A6.T12.32" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bor</span> = Borda, <span id="A6.T12.33" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Irv</span> = Instant-runoff voting, <span id="A6.T12.34" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spm</span> = Spearman, <span id="A6.T12.35" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Kem</span> = Kemeny-Young, <span id="A6.T12.36" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ken</span> = Kendall. Models: <span id="A6.T12.37" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4o11</span> = GPT-4o-2024-11-20, <span id="A6.T12.38" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4o05</span> = GPT-4o-2024-05-13, <span id="A6.T12.39" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4o08</span> = GPT-4o-2024-08-06, <span id="A6.T12.40" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sn10</span> = Claude-3.5-Sonnet-20241022, <span id="A6.T12.41" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hk10</span> = Claude-3.5-Haiku-20241022, <span id="A6.T12.42" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Op02</span> = Claude-3-Opus-20240229. Darker orange indicates stronger alignment with human judgment, with deeper hues highlighting higher correlation values.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Supplementary experiment on Q2</h2>

<figure id="A7.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15746v1/self-others-1.png" id="A7.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/173;" width="238" height="173" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span><span id="A7.F5.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Alignment with Human Judgments under Different Evaluation Protocols.</span> This figure reports the distribution of Pearson correlation coefficients between model-generated rankings and human preferences (from Chatbot Arena) across seven benchmarks under four evaluation protocols: <span id="A7.F5.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SE</span> (Self-Evaluation), <span id="A7.F5.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PE</span> (Peer Evaluation), <span id="A7.F5.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SIE</span> (Self-Inclusive Evaluation), and <span id="A7.F5.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SFE</span> (Self-Free Evaluation). In each boxplot, a <span id="A7.F5.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">higher</span> box indicates stronger agreement with human rankings, while a <span id="A7.F5.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">shorter</span> box implies lower variance and thus more stable alignment. Compared to SE and PE, the SIE and SFE protocols yield both higher and tighter boxes, suggesting that game-theoretic aggregation not only enhances ranking accuracy but also improves robustness against self-bias. Additional results are provided in the appendix due to space constraints.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A7.T13" class="ltx_table">
